# Keep the build context small and keep secrets out of the image.
#
# `vendor/` is excluded on purpose: it is built inside the image by the `build`
# stage. Copying a host vendor tree would silently produce an image whose
# dependencies were resolved against a different PHP or platform than the one
# running it — and it would also copy dev-only packages into production.
#
# `migrations.sql` and the spec bundle ARE included: the schema is the source of
# truth and belongs next to the code, and it is tiny.

.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

vendor/
node_modules/

storage/logs/*
storage/framework/cache/*
storage/framework/sessions/*
storage/framework/views/*
storage/app/*
!storage/app/.gitignore

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

tests/
tools/
docs/
*.md
Мысли.md
Мысли о SEO.txt
NABILET_Core_Technical_Spec_v1.md
state-diagrams.md

docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# `docker/php/opcache.ini` is COPYed by the Dockerfile, so it must NOT be ignored
# here. The context is filtered before any COPY runs, and an ignored file makes
# the COPY fail with "file not found" rather than silently skipping it.
# (docker/nginx/ is only read by compose at run time and never enters the image.)
